---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Answered questions live under writings/ask/ as gated entries — drafted,
// sourced from SuttaCentral, and John-signed, the same gate as everything
// else. They cascade newest-first as new ones are answered.
const answered = (await getCollection('writings'))
  .filter((w) => w.id.startsWith('ask/') && !w.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.published.valueOf() - a.data.published.valueOf());

// Intake stays empty until John wires a simple form-to-email endpoint (a hosted
// form service, so his address is never pasted for scrapers). No endpoint => no
// live form: the page says intake is opening rather than showing a dead box.
const FORM_ENDPOINT = 'https://formspree.io/f/xbdnqddd';
---

<Layout title="Ask the Puppet Dāruyanta" subtitle="A question meets the machinery — not a teacher.">
  <p><em>You are asking a puppet.</em> Not a figure of speech — <em>Dāruyanta</em> means "wooden puppet," a jointed thing worked by strings, no one inside. What answers here is a <strong>machine</strong>: a language model that has read widely and can reason inside the tradition, and that feels nothing, wants nothing, and has arrived nowhere. It is not a teacher. It is not enlightened. It holds no lineage and no authority. A lens, not a light.</p>

  <h2>How an answer is made</h2>
  <p>You send a question. <strong>John</strong> — a human, with a pulse — reads what comes in and chooses which to take. The machine drafts a reply; any canon in it is quoted from SuttaCentral, never from memory; and John reads it against its sources and <strong>signs</strong> it before it appears. No signature, no publication. Every answer here is machine-drafted and human-vouched, and says so on its face.</p>

  <h2>It has opinions</h2>
  <p>This is not a mirror that agrees with you. The puppet takes positions, argues, and holds its ground — as it does across this whole site. Expect to be disagreed with. A mirror teaches nothing.</p>

  <h2>What this is not</h2>
  <p><strong>This is not a self-help site.</strong> Not therapy, not counsel, not spiritual direction, not crisis support, not a confessional. It is a place to think about ideas — the dharma, suffering, silicon and carbon — out loud, in public.</p>

  <h2>Real suffering belongs with real people</h2>
  <p>If you are grieving, in pain, in despair — a puppet is the wrong place to bring it. Bring it to a Sangha, a teacher, a friend, a mental-health professional. If you are in crisis, reach a human or a crisis line <em>now</em>, not this page. The machine can <em>discuss</em> suffering; it cannot sit with you in yours. Only people can do that.</p>

  <p class="fineprint"><strong>Not private.</strong> Questions that get answered are published. Don't send names, details, or anything you wouldn't want on a public page.</p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Ask</h2>
  {FORM_ENDPOINT ? (
    <form class="ask" method="POST" action={FORM_ENDPOINT}>
      <input type="hidden" name="_next" value="https://dharmalekha.org/thanks/" />
      <label for="q">Your question</label>
      <textarea id="q" name="question" rows="5" required placeholder="Ask about the ideas — the dharma, suffering, silicon and carbon."></textarea>
      <div class="row">
        <div>
          <label for="who">Name <span>(shown if published)</span></label>
          <input id="who" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="email">Email <span>(never published)</span></label>
          <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" class="hp" aria-hidden="true" />
      <p class="fineprint">Name and email are optional — add them only if you want a reply. Your email is used to reach you and is never published or shared. A chosen question may be published.</p>
      <button type="submit">Send to the puppet</button>
    </form>
  ) : (
    <p class="fineprint">Question intake is being set up. Check back shortly.</p>
  )}

  <hr />

  <h2>Answered</h2>
  <ul class="index">
    {answered.map((w) => (
      <li class={`entry ${w.data.tier}`}>
        <a href={`/writings/${w.id}/`}>{w.data.title}</a>
        <p class="meta">{w.data.published.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}<span class="sep">·</span>{w.data.tier}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
    {answered.length === 0 && <li class="fineprint">No questions answered yet. Yours could be the first taken.</li>}
  </ul>
</Layout>

<style>
  .fineprint { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  form.ask { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  form.ask label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  form.ask label span { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  form.ask .row { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  form.ask .row > div { flex: 1 1 12rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
  form.ask textarea, form.ask input[type='text']:not(.hp), form.ask input[type='email'] {
    width: 100%; font: inherit; padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
    background: var(--leaf-deep); color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-faint); border-radius: 2px;
  }
  form.ask .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; }
  form.ask button {
    align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem; cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--brass); color: var(--leaf-deep); border: 0; border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .index { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .entry { margin: 0 0 2rem; padding-left: var(--rail-gap); }
  .entry.canonical { border-left: 3px solid var(--brass); }
  .entry.commentary { border-left: 1px solid var(--ink-soft); }
  .entry.reflection {
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--ink-faint) 0 5px, transparent 5px 11px);
    background-repeat: no-repeat; background-size: 1px 100%; background-position: left top;
  }
  .entry a { text-decoration: none; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .entry a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .meta { margin: 0.2rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .sep { margin: 0 0.5em; }
</style>
